WEBVTT

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:26.050
Silence, puny audience!

00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:30.388
And welcome to Who Dares To Be A Millionaire?

00:00:30.472 --> 00:00:33.558
Tremble before
Morbo's mighty likability,

00:00:33.642 --> 00:00:37.395
as I chitchat with our first
contestant, Philip J. Fry.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.320
Give him hell, Morbo!

00:00:47.906 --> 00:00:50.241
Prepare for pleasantries!

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.785
So, Fry, what do you
do for a living?

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.371
Me?
Can I phone a friend?

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.789
Chitchat achieved!

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.377
Are you ready to play?

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.589
I didn't come to play,
I came to win.

00:01:04.673 --> 00:01:05.965
Now let's play.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:10.219
For $1, what tool is
used to hammer a nail?

00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:12.722
Is it, A, a hammer?

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:14.724
B, a nail?

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.601
C...
B, Nail! Final answer!

00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:22.440
Sweet dodo
of Lesotho!

00:01:22.524 --> 00:01:25.192
Don't you ever stop to think
before you speak?

00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:26.986
I never stop to
think about it.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:31.407
Leave Fry alone. His intelligence
is just a little differenty.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:33.409
You a big dummy!

00:01:33.535 --> 00:01:36.829
Hey, I'm beginning to think you
guys don't think I'm very smart.

00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:39.832
You can barely remember
your own name, Einstein.

00:01:39.917 --> 00:01:41.918
Einstein is a hard name
to remember.

00:01:42.419 --> 00:01:43.419
Ow!

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.879
Smeesh, Professor.

00:01:44.963 --> 00:01:48.090
Don't have a shmaneurysm.
Fry's your distant relative.

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:49.383
Not distant enough.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.470
I'll be a monkey's uncle
if I'm this monkey's nephew.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.848
But you're
my only family.

00:01:56.016 --> 00:01:58.726
Who will hug me if
I achieve something?

00:01:59.019 --> 00:02:01.812
Oh, perhaps
I've been too harsh.

00:02:02.105 --> 00:02:07.526
Come, lad, take my hand and I'll
explain why I find you so repugnant.

00:02:08.487 --> 00:02:12.114
All my life, I've been
inspired by great minds.

00:02:12.574 --> 00:02:15.826
Euclid, Copernicus, Braino.

00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:20.039
And my personal role model,
Leonardo da Vinci.

00:02:20.499 --> 00:02:22.083
What turned them to stone?

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:26.045
Da Vinci was history's
greatest artist and inventor.

00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:30.675
Voilа!

00:02:30.759 --> 00:02:35.096
He invented flying machines,
war engines, submarines.

00:02:35.222 --> 00:02:37.431
Uh-oh. Nibbler died in the wall.

00:02:37.516 --> 00:02:40.810
That's not Nibbler. That's
my most precious possession.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.561
Leonardo's beard!

00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:46.732
I paid a fortune for it at an
auction of historic body parts.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.194
I suppose if I have
an Achilles' heel,

00:02:50.278 --> 00:02:53.030
it's because I bought it
at that same auction.

00:02:53.407 --> 00:02:57.284
Indeed so.
Most indeededly.

00:02:57.369 --> 00:02:58.953
Careful with that,
you fool!

00:03:00.414 --> 00:03:03.499
No! No!

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:05.751
But possibly yes.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:07.753
What is it, Professor?

00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:14.677
Oh, my! It's da Vinci's
fabled lost invention.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:19.598
Even the scholars who wrote of this
device had no idea what it was for.

00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:22.643
And now, at last,
neither do I!

00:03:22.728 --> 00:03:24.020
Maybe we can
figure it out.

00:03:24.104 --> 00:03:26.605
We?

00:03:28.108 --> 00:03:30.234
Well, I may not
have brain smarts,

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.486
but at least
I have street smarts.

00:03:35.991 --> 00:03:38.743
I was in the hospital two
weeks. No one visited me.

00:03:38.827 --> 00:03:39.952
Quiet, you!

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.123
I'm trying to deduce the function
of da Vinci's lost invention.

00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:45.499
Not even a card.

00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:48.502
He might have hidden a clue
in one of his other works.

00:03:48.587 --> 00:03:52.465
Ergo, I sent Bender out for
a copy of The Last Supper.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:53.632
I'm back!

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.470
Everybody at Kinko's was an idiot,
so I just brought the original.

00:04:04.728 --> 00:04:08.147
Jesus Christ,
and his 12 Apostles.

00:04:08.315 --> 00:04:09.398
That's odd.

00:04:09.483 --> 00:04:12.276
This hand here doesn't
belong to anybody.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.071
And it's pointing a knife
at James the Lesser!

00:04:15.155 --> 00:04:17.073
That's the great thing
about that hand.

00:04:17.157 --> 00:04:19.617
And what about
these funky table legs?

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:22.411
It's like they're from
some other, funkier painting.

00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:25.081
Maybe da Vinci painted
over something else.

00:04:25.165 --> 00:04:26.791
It's called a pentimento.

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:30.669
That's true, Dr. Zoidberg.
How did you know that?

00:04:30.754 --> 00:04:32.922
My doctorate is
in art history.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.341
Let's see what's
under The Last Supper.

00:04:39.096 --> 00:04:42.389
Wait a second! I'm not big-boned, I'm just fat.

00:04:44.142 --> 00:04:45.893
My God! Look!

00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:48.979
My God! I'm looking!

00:04:50.732 --> 00:04:53.651
My God! Saint James was a robot!

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:57.488
My God! Da Vinci left his
legs unpainted as a clue.

00:04:57.614 --> 00:05:01.826
My God! This is the greatest mystery of all time.

00:05:01.993 --> 00:05:05.746
We must fly to Rome and
exhume the body of Saint James.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.749
Didn't we used to be a
delivery company? To the ship.

00:05:40.282 --> 00:05:41.323
Psst.

00:05:41.408 --> 00:05:43.951
Leela, wanna join
the mile-deep club?

00:05:44.035 --> 00:05:45.744
Sure, why not?

00:05:45.829 --> 00:05:47.997
No time!
I've found a clue that

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:50.749
could unlock all
the secrets of history.

00:05:52.252 --> 00:05:54.295
Look at these
Roman numerals.

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:55.504
Roman numerals?

00:05:55.881 --> 00:05:57.756
I've got it!
We're in Rome!

00:05:57.841 --> 00:06:01.760
Don't be stupid. It's a
long-lost mathematical code.

00:06:01.845 --> 00:06:04.930
I'll need to consult
these ancient writings.

00:06:08.476 --> 00:06:13.606
Some preposterous hogwash
about the Fibonacci sequence...

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:14.690
Aha!

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:18.277
The markings indicate how
many paces we need to take.

00:06:19.487 --> 00:06:22.740
One... Okay,
we're there.

00:06:24.075 --> 00:06:26.243
Brothers and sisters,
let us pry.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:35.586
It's true! Saint James
really was a robot.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:40.257
I bet he's up in robot heaven right
now. So he won't miss his eyes.

00:06:51.436 --> 00:06:54.980
My God! Robot Saint
James is a zombie.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:57.816
Nay, I am not Saint James.

00:06:57.901 --> 00:06:59.777
Enough of your lies,
Saint James.

00:06:59.903 --> 00:07:01.820
We saw you in
The Last Supper.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:05.783
The great man Leonardo built
me as an artist's model.

00:07:05.867 --> 00:07:07.451
When I took repose
in this coffin,

00:07:07.744 --> 00:07:11.163
I carefully tossed the real
Saint James in yonder heap.

00:07:12.457 --> 00:07:14.583
I'm sure you have
many questions.

00:07:14.668 --> 00:07:16.752
Come, there is a chamber where I used to

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:18.796
speak with Pope John
the Patient.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.343
I told him I'd be
back in five minutes.

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:26.762
Well, he'll make
a nice heap.

00:07:30.475 --> 00:07:35.062
I am Animatronio, guardian
of da Vinci's great secret.

00:07:35.146 --> 00:07:37.856
He left my legs visible
in the painting as a clue,

00:07:37.941 --> 00:07:40.025
then dispatched me
hither to await

00:07:40.151 --> 00:07:43.153
his shadow society
of intellectuals.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.155
Hi, Animatronio.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.950
You personally
knew da Vinci?

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:51.453
Was he nice?
How did his hair smell?

00:07:51.538 --> 00:07:55.040
And on a personal note, what
is the function of this device?

00:07:55.125 --> 00:07:58.877
Halt! You know not the function
of the machina magnifica?

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:02.298
Then thou art not members
of the shadow society!

00:08:02.382 --> 00:08:03.424
The what now?

00:08:03.508 --> 00:08:05.509
Not one more word
shall I breathe.

00:08:05.593 --> 00:08:08.846
Not even about the great fountain
where thou mayest find the...

00:08:09.514 --> 00:08:10.514
Wait...

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.726
Thou didst not know about
the fountain, didst thou?

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.936
Curses!
I must be punished.

00:08:18.648 --> 00:08:20.482
Quick, we must
find out what he knows

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.693
before he flays
himself to death!

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.278
Where is the
great fountain?

00:08:24.362 --> 00:08:25.446
What makes it so great?

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.323
Why does a robot
need a codpiece?

00:08:27.407 --> 00:08:29.867
Fie, thou
fen-suckled bum-bailey!

00:08:29.951 --> 00:08:33.662
Thou willst never pry information
from these mechanical lips!

00:08:33.747 --> 00:08:35.289
Just tell us, already.

00:08:35.373 --> 00:08:37.666
Okay, the fountain
thou seekest is...

00:08:40.837 --> 00:08:44.089
And so dies our hope
of solving this mystery.

00:08:44.382 --> 00:08:46.842
Come on, gang.
Let's go home.

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:49.136
Wait! Let's not
give up so easily.

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:51.555
Animatronio
mentioned a fountain.

00:08:51.973 --> 00:08:54.975
That's a statue of Neptune,
god of water.

00:08:55.101 --> 00:08:58.854
The number of points on his
trident is three, or trey.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:01.774
The "U" in his name
is written like "V".

00:09:01.858 --> 00:09:03.525
Trey, "V".

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.071
Trevi!
It's the Trevi fountain!

00:09:07.155 --> 00:09:10.115
There can be no question! But, Professor...

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.784
There can be no question!

00:09:13.453 --> 00:09:16.538
Wow, it hasn't changed
in 1,000 years.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.711
Okay, everyone,
into the fountain.

00:09:22.796 --> 00:09:25.339
What are you, senile?
I'm not jumping in there.

00:09:25.423 --> 00:09:26.673
Hey, look. Coins.

00:09:48.947 --> 00:09:50.322
I got 48 cents.

00:09:50.865 --> 00:09:53.951
There's one more nickel,
and it's a big one!

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:10.759
Quickly,
into the sewer hole.

00:10:13.847 --> 00:10:14.888
Why?

00:10:29.988 --> 00:10:31.238
What's this dump?

00:10:38.872 --> 00:10:41.832
My God!
It's the Pantheon!

00:10:41.916 --> 00:10:44.293
This place is
3,000 years old.

00:10:44.377 --> 00:10:46.587
What could possibly
be left to discover?

00:10:46.671 --> 00:10:49.631
Maybe something
about ourselves, Leela.

00:10:49.716 --> 00:10:51.383
Wait!
What's under that blanket?

00:10:52.927 --> 00:10:56.430
My God!
Da Vinci's Vitruvian Man!

00:10:56.764 --> 00:10:58.599
It's truly a masterpiece.

00:10:58.683 --> 00:11:00.225
Note how
the perspective lines

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.144
draw the eye
right to his dong.

00:11:04.314 --> 00:11:05.898
Say, what's this?

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:08.525
Anyone hear something?

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.068
It's a coin slot.

00:11:10.153 --> 00:11:12.488
Bender,
insert that giant nickel.

00:11:12.572 --> 00:11:13.739
Sure.

00:11:18.286 --> 00:11:20.078
Hush, Bender!

00:11:21.623 --> 00:11:24.291
What's your game,
Vitruvian Man?

00:11:30.256 --> 00:11:31.590
Whoa!
Whoa!

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.136
I withdraw
the question, Vitruvian Man.

00:11:37.055 --> 00:11:39.932
Da Vinci's lost workshop!

00:11:40.225 --> 00:11:41.725
At the risk of
sounding stupid,

00:11:41.851 --> 00:11:43.352
do these things
actually work?

00:11:43.436 --> 00:11:45.187
Of course not, stupid!

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:49.274
I mean, that flying machine's
as aerodynamic as a sofa!

00:11:49.359 --> 00:11:52.110
How could it possibly
get off the ground?

00:11:52.195 --> 00:11:54.988
In a way thou shalt
never discover!

00:11:57.867 --> 00:11:59.201
Hi, Animatronio.

00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:01.370
I feign death
and stalk thee,

00:12:01.454 --> 00:12:04.540
that I might preserve the
greatest of Leonardo's secrets!

00:12:09.754 --> 00:12:13.674
All right, buddy, we want secrets
! And they'd better be ancient!

00:12:15.635 --> 00:12:19.555
Never shall I reveal how these
wondrous machines fit together!

00:12:19.639 --> 00:12:21.098
They fit together?

00:12:21.182 --> 00:12:23.475
I said no such thing.
And then I died!

00:12:27.981 --> 00:12:30.440
You're right, Professor.
This thing doesn't fly.

00:12:30.525 --> 00:12:33.360
Don't sit in there, you idiot! That's dangerous!

00:12:56.676 --> 00:13:00.679
No wonder this contraption isn't aerodynamic!

00:13:00.763 --> 00:13:03.724
It's not an aircraft,
it's a spacecraft!

00:13:05.852 --> 00:13:09.187
As I live, thou shan't
discover the great secret!

00:13:16.154 --> 00:13:18.030
Bye, Animatronio!

00:13:45.933 --> 00:13:47.142
My God!

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:50.270
Why would Leonardo's machine
have brought us here?

00:13:50.355 --> 00:13:52.898
I don't know.
Let's ask this guy.

00:13:53.024 --> 00:13:55.233
I am Leonardo.

00:13:56.694 --> 00:13:58.737
Welcome to Planet Vinci.

00:14:03.284 --> 00:14:05.202
My God!

00:14:05.328 --> 00:14:07.245
That's what
I was gonna say!

00:14:15.922 --> 00:14:19.424
Leonardo!
You're alive? Here?

00:14:20.593 --> 00:14:24.805
You've learned my great secret.
I was but a visitor to Earth.

00:14:24.889 --> 00:14:28.141
In truth, I am what
you call a space alien.

00:14:28.309 --> 00:14:29.351
Oh!

00:14:29.435 --> 00:14:31.019
It's an honor to
meet you, Leonardo.

00:14:31.104 --> 00:14:35.190
And may I say, you were
great in Titanic. The Beach...

00:14:35.274 --> 00:14:38.235
That's Leonardo DiCaprio,
you blockhead!

00:14:40.238 --> 00:14:42.823
Looks like eating rocks
wasn't as dumb as you said.

00:14:46.536 --> 00:14:48.161
So what do people
do for fun here?

00:14:48.246 --> 00:14:50.497
Do you enjoy
partying all night,

00:14:50.623 --> 00:14:52.916
with plenty of ale
and lusty women?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.001
I sure do!
Not us.

00:14:55.086 --> 00:14:58.714
We spend our leisure time
in the mathematics museum.

00:15:00.425 --> 00:15:04.594
Planet Vinci is basically
a single colossal university.

00:15:04.929 --> 00:15:06.263
How's your football team?

00:15:06.347 --> 00:15:07.472
Learned.

00:15:07.557 --> 00:15:10.642
Ooh! I'm going to check out
that math lecture.

00:15:10.727 --> 00:15:14.312
All this knowledge is giving me a raging brainer.

00:15:14.814 --> 00:15:17.524
Would you like to hear
the lecture, too, Fry?

00:15:17.608 --> 00:15:20.569
No. It would just go in one
ear and out some other hole.

00:15:20.778 --> 00:15:22.487
Come. Sit down.

00:15:22.822 --> 00:15:24.865
Now, that I can do.

00:15:25.533 --> 00:15:28.910
I have a terrible secret
to confess, Mr. DiCaprio.

00:15:28.995 --> 00:15:30.412
I'm not very smart.

00:15:30.496 --> 00:15:32.414
I appreciate your candor.

00:15:33.291 --> 00:15:36.001
I don't even know what
language you're speaking.

00:15:37.378 --> 00:15:39.755
I, too, have a confession.

00:15:39.839 --> 00:15:44.509
You see, here on Planet Vinci,
I am the stupidest person.

00:15:44.844 --> 00:15:47.429
What? Who'd possibly
think you're stupid?

00:15:47.513 --> 00:15:49.264
Duh! I'm Leonardo!

00:15:49.348 --> 00:15:51.808
I don't know the mass
of the Higgs boson.

00:15:51.893 --> 00:15:54.352
Duh!
I have to draw in pencil,

00:15:54.437 --> 00:15:57.689
'cause I don't know how to
use rendering software.

00:16:00.943 --> 00:16:03.945
Stupid Biff!
Thinks he's so smart.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:05.530
He looks stronger
than you, too.

00:16:05.615 --> 00:16:09.576
I went to Earth because I could
no longer stand the ridicule.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:14.664
But being surrounded by even stupider
people was equally infuriating.

00:16:15.041 --> 00:16:17.209
I can see myself
in your shiny button.

00:16:17.293 --> 00:16:19.544
Inventing is
what makes me happy.

00:16:19.629 --> 00:16:23.089
Or did, until I misplaced
the plans for my masterpiece.

00:16:23.216 --> 00:16:24.341
You mean these?

00:16:24.425 --> 00:16:27.594
The machina magnifica?

00:16:28.137 --> 00:16:29.679
Infinite joy!

00:16:29.931 --> 00:16:33.475
Fry, my friend, you have
given my life meaning again!

00:16:33.768 --> 00:16:36.978
That calculus lecture
was harder than I expected.

00:16:37.063 --> 00:16:40.440
We had to answer every question
in the form of an opera.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.526
I have a lot of
homework for tomorrow,

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:46.488
if I don't want
to be embarrassed.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.583
Thank you. Thank you.

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:42.377
And if you like that,
you'll love our main event.

00:17:42.503 --> 00:17:46.464
Ladies and gentlemen,
Leonardo DiCaprio!

00:17:48.926 --> 00:17:50.594
I mean, da Vinci!

00:17:54.974 --> 00:17:59.728
For centuries, you've ridiculed
me. Especially you, Biff.

00:17:59.896 --> 00:18:01.062
Nice hat!

00:18:02.982 --> 00:18:06.985
But, at long last, this invention will show you.

00:18:07.278 --> 00:18:08.653
It will show you all!

00:18:09.447 --> 00:18:13.825
Behold, my unstoppable
doomsday machine!

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:15.160
And I helped!

00:18:15.453 --> 00:18:18.663
Wait. You told me it was an
unstoppable ice cream machine.

00:18:18.873 --> 00:18:21.625
Ice cream is just a by-product of the machine!

00:18:21.709 --> 00:18:24.544
Its primary purpose
is to exterminate

00:18:24.629 --> 00:18:27.380
everyone who ever
made me feel inferior!

00:18:27.548 --> 00:18:30.842
Ooh! I'm so scared!

00:18:31.052 --> 00:18:33.178
Bring it on, dum-dum!

00:18:36.891 --> 00:18:39.434
Oh, yeah? Let's see how
hard you're laughing

00:18:39.518 --> 00:18:42.687
when my doomsday machine
chops off your face!

00:18:54.575 --> 00:18:56.117
Leonardo, stop!

00:18:57.453 --> 00:18:59.037
I want in on this!

00:18:59.413 --> 00:19:01.081
Are you crazy, Professor?

00:19:01.165 --> 00:19:02.874
I hate these nerds!

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.793
Just 'cause I'm
stupider than them,

00:19:04.877 --> 00:19:07.170
they think they're smarter than me.

00:19:07.254 --> 00:19:10.715
Kill them all, starting with the math teacher!

00:19:24.355 --> 00:19:28.024
I knew this final invention
would be a humdinger.

00:19:28.109 --> 00:19:32.278
Yes. We three idiots will
finally have our revenge!

00:19:32.655 --> 00:19:34.280
I don't think so.

00:19:34.532 --> 00:19:38.576
You two make me ashamed
to call myself an idiot.

00:19:42.915 --> 00:19:45.000
There's always going to be
someone smarter than you,

00:19:45.084 --> 00:19:48.253
so the only way to be happy is to
make the most of what you've got.

00:19:48.337 --> 00:19:49.629
But you've got nothing.

00:19:49.714 --> 00:19:50.755
Oh, no?

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:54.884
I've got one single nail, and
another nail to nail it in with.

00:19:54.969 --> 00:19:58.430
And I'm gonna stop this infernal
ice cream machine once and for all!

00:20:20.995 --> 00:20:24.372
Some doomsday machine!
It barely killed anyone!

00:20:24.457 --> 00:20:25.540
Oh, yeah?

00:20:26.709 --> 00:20:27.959
Well, take this!

00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:31.796
Oh, my.

00:20:32.173 --> 00:20:36.593
Poor Leonardo da Vinci.
He sure was stupid.

00:20:39.513 --> 00:20:42.515
Fry, I admire
what you did today,

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:46.061
and I'm deeply sorry for
insulting your intellect.

00:20:46.145 --> 00:20:48.813
Your tiny, tiny intellect.

00:20:48.898 --> 00:20:50.857
Oops. There I go again,
you dope.

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:52.233
I mean, dummy.

00:20:52.318 --> 00:20:53.318
It's okay.

00:20:53.402 --> 00:20:55.945
I may not be clever,
but I have a good heart.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:57.739
That's what my mom
used to say.

00:20:57.823 --> 00:20:59.991
She was a wise woman.

00:21:00.201 --> 00:21:02.202
Also, that I'm not
much to look at.

00:21:02.286 --> 00:21:05.038
A wise woman, indeed.